{"id":"h0-03-f3","title":"Back-of-envelope estimation","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: QPS, peak, storage, bandwidth and server sizing with worked examples. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"why-estimate-at-all","title":"Why estimate at all","html":"<p><strong>Back-of-envelope estimation turns \"lots of users\" into numbers that choose the architecture.</strong> Nobody checks your arithmetic to the digit. They check that you know which numbers matter and that the result changes what you build.</p>\n<p>Three questions to answer: how many requests per second (QPS), how much storage, how much bandwidth.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 476.8 192\" width=\"476.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Estimation ends in design decisions\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 96 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 96 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 158 L304 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 158 L304 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Users</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">QPS</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Storage</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"136\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Bandwidth</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"384.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Servers and DB type</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"74\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"384.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Sharding and tiers</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"136\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"384.4\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">CDN and network</text></svg><figcaption>Estimation ends in design decisions</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 1M requests/s means a fleet and sharding. 50 requests/s means one small server. Both are \"a web app\", but the designs are nothing alike. The estimate tells you which problem you have.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Jeff Dean's \"numbers every engineer should know\" (see next note) is the origin of this habit at Google. Capacity planning at Netflix and Uber starts from the same arithmetic, then adds load tests.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Before a wedding you count guests to decide the venue size; you do not weigh the rice.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Skipping estimates entirely or spending 15 minutes on them.</li>\n<li>Using unrounded numbers like 86,413 seconds; use 86,400 or even 100,000 for quick maths.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"handy-constants-and-rounding","title":"Handy constants and rounding","html":"<p><strong>Round aggressively; keep powers of ten in your head.</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Seconds per day      86,400   (~ 10^5)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Seconds per month    2.6M     (~ 2.5 x 10^6)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Seconds per year     31.5M    (~ 3 x 10^7)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>1 KB = 10^3 B, 1 MB = 10^6, 1 GB = 10^9, 1 TB = 10^12, 1 PB = 10^15</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>1M req/day  ~ 12 req/s</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>100M req/day ~ 1,160 req/s ~ 1.2K/s</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>1B req/day  ~ 11,600 req/s ~ 12K/s</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 524.8000000000001 68\" width=\"524.8000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Rule: per-day to per-second, divide by 10^5\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M151.2 34 L207.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M151.2 34 L207.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M353.6 34 L409.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M353.6 34 L409.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"81.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Requests per day</text><rect x=\"207.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"280.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Divide by 100,000</text><rect x=\"409.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"461.20000000000005\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Average QPS</text></svg><figcaption>Rule: per-day to per-second, divide by 10^5</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Shortcut: <strong>requests/day divided by 100,000 = average QPS</strong> (slightly low, which the peak factor corrects).</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 300M requests/day / 10^5 = 3,000 QPS. Exact: 300M / 86,400 = 3,472. The shortcut is within 15%, good enough.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Twitter once quoted about 500M tweets/day, which is about 5,800 tweets/s average; reads are far larger.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Estimating a drive: \"100 km at 50 km/h is 2 hours\" without looking at the map.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mixing bits and bytes: network is quoted in bits (Mbps), storage in bytes. Divide Mbps by 8.</li>\n<li>Mixing 1000 and 1024; for estimates it does not matter, so do not argue about it.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"qps-and-peak","title":"QPS and peak","html":"<p><strong>Average QPS = daily actions / 86,400. Peak is higher: use 2x to 3x for normal products, 10x or more for spiky ones (sales, live events).</strong></p>\n<p>Steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>DAU (daily active users).</li>\n<li>Actions per user per day, separately for reads and writes.</li>\n<li>Total per day, divide by 10^5 (or 86,400).</li>\n<li>Multiply by peak factor.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 788 68\" width=\"788\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"From DAU to peak QPS\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 34 L353.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 34 L353.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M470.8 34 L526.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M470.8 34 L526.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M630 34 L686 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M630 34 L686 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">DAU</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Actions per user</text><rect x=\"353.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"412\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Per day total</text><rect x=\"526.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"578.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Average QPS</text><rect x=\"686\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"731\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Peak QPS</text></svg><figcaption>From DAU to peak QPS</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example (Twitter-like).</strong> 200M DAU. Each user reads the timeline 20 times (200 tweets total) and posts 0.5 tweets/day.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Timeline loads: 200M x 20 = 4B/day = 46,000/s average, 3x peak is about 140,000/s.</li>\n<li>Tweets written: 200M x 0.5 = 100M/day = 1,160/s, peak about 3,500/s.</li>\n<li>Read:write is about 40:1. So: heavy caching, read replicas, fan-out cache; writes fit comfortably on a small sharded cluster.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Flash sales (Flipkart Big Billion Days, Amazon Prime Day) can reach 10x to 50x normal; companies pre-scale and queue rather than size for average. IPL streaming (Hotstar) planned for tens of millions of concurrent viewers.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> The peak factor you pick is a cost decision, reversible with autoscaling but not instantly: if cold starts take minutes, a sudden 10x spike still hurts. State the factor and whether you will pre-scale.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A road is designed for rush hour, not for 3 a.m. traffic.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Using average QPS to size capacity.</li>\n<li>Treating all requests as equal; a search call may cost 100x a cached read.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"storage-estimation","title":"Storage estimation","html":"<p><strong>Storage = number of items x size per item x retention x replication factor.</strong> Remember indexes and metadata add 20 to 100% overhead.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 912.4000000000001 68\" width=\"912.4000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Storage builds up from the item size\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M129.60000000000002 34 L185.60000000000002 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M129.60000000000002 34 L185.60000000000002 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M449.20000000000005 34 L505.20000000000005 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M449.20000000000005 34 L505.20000000000005 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M595.2 34 L651.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M595.2 34 L651.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M754.4000000000001 34 L810.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M754.4000000000001 34 L810.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"70.80000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Items per day</text><rect x=\"185.60000000000002\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"230.60000000000002\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Item size</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"390.40000000000003\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Per day bytes</text><rect x=\"505.20000000000005\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"550.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Retention</text><rect x=\"651.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"702.8000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replication</text><rect x=\"810.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"855.4000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Total</text></svg><figcaption>Storage builds up from the item size</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example (photo app).</strong> 10M new photos/day, 2 MB original plus 3 thumbnails totalling 300 KB: about 2.3 MB per photo. Per day: 10M x 2.3 MB = 23 TB. Per year: 23 TB x 365 = 8.4 PB. With 3x replication (or about 1.5x with erasure coding): 25 PB or 12.6 PB. Metadata rows (200 bytes each) are only 10M x 200 B = 2 GB/day, trivial next to the blobs. Conclusion: blobs go to object storage (S3-like), metadata in a database; storage cost, not compute, is the biggest bill.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example (messages).</strong> 2B messages/day x 100 bytes = 200 GB/day = 73 TB/year. Fits a sharded database easily; keep 1 year hot and archive older to cheaper storage.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Facebook's Haystack and f4 papers describe cutting blob storage cost with log-structured stores and erasure coding for warm photos. Dropbox's Magic Pocket moved from S3 to its own storage for cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Filling shelves: shelf space needed is books per year times thickness times years kept.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forgetting replication (3x is the usual default).</li>\n<li>Forgetting that video or images dwarf text; do blobs and metadata separately.</li>\n<li>Not stating retention; \"forever\" is an expensive assumption.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"bandwidth-estimation","title":"Bandwidth estimation","html":"<p><strong>Bandwidth = QPS x payload size, in and out separately. Convert bytes to bits (x8) when comparing to network links.</strong></p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 858.8 68\" width=\"858.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bandwidth is rate times size\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M268.4 34 L324.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M268.4 34 L324.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M463.59999999999997 34 L519.5999999999999 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M463.59999999999997 34 L519.5999999999999 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M651.5999999999999 34 L707.5999999999999 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M651.5999999999999 34 L707.5999999999999 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Peak QPS</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Payload size</text><rect x=\"324.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Bytes per second</text><rect x=\"519.5999999999999\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"585.5999999999999\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Bits per second</text><rect x=\"707.5999999999999\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"777.1999999999999\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">NIC and CDN plan</text></svg><figcaption>Bandwidth is rate times size</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example (video).</strong> 5M concurrent viewers at 3 Mbps average (720p-ish) = 15 Tbps. No origin can serve that; it demands a CDN. A single 25 Gbps server NIC delivers about 8,000 such streams, so you would need about 600 servers for all 5M if there were no CDN. This is why Netflix pushes Open Connect boxes into ISPs.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example (API).</strong> 70,000 read QPS x 5 KB response = 350 MB/s = 2.8 Gbps. A few 10 Gbps load balancers handle it. Upload side: 3,500 writes/s x 2 KB = 7 MB/s, negligible.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Netflix and YouTube serve most bytes from caches near users. Cloud providers charge for egress (roughly cents per GB), so bandwidth is also a cost line.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Choosing a CDN is reversible (swap providers by DNS and config), while choosing to host your own edge is a one-way capital door.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Water pipes: flow equals how many taps open times the water each uses.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mbps vs MBps confusion (factor of 8).</li>\n<li>Ignoring that egress costs money.</li>\n<li>Using the same payload size for requests and responses.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"server-and-memory-estimation","title":"Server and memory estimation","html":"<p><strong>Servers needed = peak QPS / QPS per server, plus headroom (30 to 50%) and N+1 for failures.</strong> Memory for cache = hot working set size.</p>\n<p>Rules of thumb (confirm by load test): a tuned app server handles 500 to 5,000 simple requests/s per core-pair depending on work; a Postgres primary handles a few thousand simple writes/s and perhaps 10K to 50K simple indexed reads/s; Redis handles on the order of 100K ops/s per node; Kafka partitions handle tens of MB/s each.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 789.1999999999999 68\" width=\"789.1999999999999\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sizing flow\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M318.8 34 L374.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M318.8 34 L374.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M464.8 34 L520.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M464.8 34 L520.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M631.1999999999999 34 L687.1999999999999 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M631.1999999999999 34 L687.1999999999999 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Peak QPS</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"238.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Per-server capacity</text><rect x=\"374.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"419.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Count</text><rect x=\"520.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"576\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Add headroom</text><rect x=\"687.1999999999999\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"732.1999999999999\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Add N+1</text></svg><figcaption>Sizing flow</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example (cache sizing).</strong> Feed of 100M users, cache the latest 500 post IDs (8 bytes each) for the 20% active: 20M x 500 x 8 B = 80 GB. With Redis overhead say 120 GB: two 64 GB nodes would be too tight; use 4 nodes of 64 GB (about 2x spare) with replicas.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example (app tier).</strong> Peak 140,000 read QPS, each server handles 3,000 QPS. 140,000 / 3,000 = 47 servers, with 40% headroom about 66, spread across 3 zones (22 each so losing a zone leaves 44, which is borderline; add a few more).</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Stack Overflow publishes its server counts (a small number of beefy machines serving huge traffic). Twitter, Instagram have shared cache hit ratio targets above 95%.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Staffing a call centre: calls per hour divided by calls an agent handles, plus a few spare for sick days.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Quoting a specific per-server QPS as fact; say \"assume, then validate with a load test\".</li>\n<li>Forgetting zone-failure headroom.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"a-full-worked-example-url-shortener","title":"A full worked example: URL shortener","html":"<p><strong>Put it all together in four lines.</strong></p>\n<p>Assumptions: 100M new URLs/day, read:write 100:1, keep 5 years, 500 bytes per record.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Writes:   100M / 86,400        = ~1,200/s    peak ~3,600/s</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Reads:    100x writes          = ~120,000/s  peak ~360,000/s</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Storage:  100M x 365 x 5       = 182.5B rows</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>          x 500 B              = ~91 TB  (x3 replicas = ~270 TB)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Bandwidth (read, 500 B resp):  120,000 x 500 B = 60 MB/s = 0.5 Gbps (tiny)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Short key length: 62^7 = 3.5 trillion > 182B  -> 7 chars is enough</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 934 68\" width=\"934\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Estimates point to a cache-heavy KV design\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M421.6 34 L477.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M421.6 34 L477.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M580.8000000000001 34 L636.8000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M580.8000000000001 34 L636.8000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M726.8000000000001 34 L782.8000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M726.8000000000001 34 L782.8000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">CDN</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Load balancer</text><rect x=\"477.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"529.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App servers</text><rect x=\"636.8000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"681.8000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Cache</text><rect x=\"782.8000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"852.4000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Sharded KV store</text></svg><figcaption>Estimates point to a cache-heavy KV design</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Conclusions: reads dominate so cache hot links (80/20 rule: cache 20% of daily reads); 91 TB is too big for one node, shard by short key hash; bandwidth is small, so no special network plan.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Bitly and TinyURL style services; real ones use key-value stores such as DynamoDB, Cassandra or sharded MySQL.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A library catalogue: lookups are constant, new books arrive slowly.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Using 7-char keys without showing 62^7 (that number is worth memorising).</li>\n<li>Forgetting that cache hit ratio changes DB QPS: at 90% hit ratio the DB sees only 10% of reads (12,000/s).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"sanity-checks-and-communicating-estimates","title":"Sanity checks and communicating estimates","html":"<p><strong>State assumptions, show arithmetic, round, then say what the number implies.</strong> Cross-check with a known system: if your chat app needs more messages/s than WhatsApp's published scale with 1% of its users, you made an error.</p>\n<p>Habits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Write units on every line (QPS, GB/day, Mbps).</li>\n<li>Do reads and writes separately.</li>\n<li>Ask the interviewer to confirm assumptions rather than guessing silently.</li>\n<li>Stop when you know the design consequence; do not keep multiplying.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 663.6 68\" width=\"663.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Estimate, then conclude\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M267.2 34 L323.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M267.2 34 L323.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M413.2 34 L469.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M413.2 34 L469.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Assumptions</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"219.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Arithmetic</text><rect x=\"323.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"368.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Round</text><rect x=\"469.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"182.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"560.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Implication for design</text></svg><figcaption>Estimate, then conclude</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> \"So peak is about 10K QPS, which a handful of stateless servers and one Postgres with replicas can serve; I will not shard yet.\" That sentence, not the digits, is what scores.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Google SRE books describe the same approach in capacity planning: estimate, then validate with load tests and real traffic.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Estimating cooking time: \"about 20 minutes\", then check with a fork.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Silent arithmetic; the interviewer cannot give credit for what they cannot hear.</li>\n<li>Ending with a number and no conclusion.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Estimate QPS, storage, bandwidth, servers; use numbers to choose the design.</li>\n<li>Per-day to per-second: divide by 10^5. Peak = 2x to 3x (more for spiky traffic).</li>\n<li>Storage = items x size x retention x replication; separate blobs from metadata.</li>\n<li>Bandwidth: bytes x 8 for bits; video needs a CDN.</li>\n<li>Servers: peak QPS / per-server capacity + headroom + zone failure.</li>\n<li>Always finish with what the number implies; round and state assumptions.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}